I played 241 games of nethack before my first ascension. I never quit
because of bad stats/starting items (IMHO there are so many other
random effects, these don't matter too much - just alter your playstyle).
I never read a spoiler file,  but read some general spoilers on here. I
did not learn the bell/book/candle trick here - I genuinely learnt it
from the oracle before ever I'd even seen medusa.

I made *lots* of mistakes in my first ascension - esp in the elemental
planes, where I didn't know what I was doing. It cost me 5 exp levels
and lots of equipment, but I feel that a character who's survived the
quest can deal with most things other than instant-death. (eg cockatrice).
(Oh, about the bell/book/candle _ i think the oracle is a bit misleading.
I cocked up multiple times and posted a plea here - which i then cancelled,
as I figured it out by myself).

I play an ultra-cautious game - I don't generally try things just to see
what they are - I wait till I have a bushell of id scrolls (which are a
pain to id themselves - one of the things I *did* learn through spoiling
is their cheapness in shops, which is what I use.)

I have never wished for an item I have not come across at sometime, and
never wished for an artifact (personally, I think it should be
impossible to wish for artifacts - they should be precious things, earned
through great sacrifice, struggle, or luck.)

